# 1Password

Cross-platform password manager and passkey vault for iOS, macOS, Windows, Android, and Linux.

- **Website:** [1password.com](https://1password.com)
- **App Store:** [1Password - Password Manager](https://apple.com)
- **Initial Release:** May 2006
- **Developer:** 1Password (formerly AgileBits)

---

## About

1Password started in 2005 as a small Mac utility built by AgileBits to automate form-filling while testing websites. Over the last two decades, it has grown from local encrypted vault files into a full cloud-synced password manager, passkey vault, and developer secrets tool.

---

## History

- **2005–2006 — Early Mac days:** Canadian developers Dave Teare and Roustem Karimov founded Agile Web Solutions (later AgileBits) in 2005 and released the first public Mac version, originally spelled *1Passwd*, in May 2006.
- **2008–2013 — Going mobile:** After Apple launched the iPhone SDK in 2008, 1Password became one of the first password managers on the iOS App Store. Windows and Android apps followed, using Dropbox and Wi-Fi syncing to keep local vault files updated across devices.
- **2016–2018 — Cloud accounts and rebrand:** In 2016, the company launched hosted cloud accounts and introduced its Secret Key encryption model. By late 2018, AgileBits officially renamed itself to 1Password and moved from one-time license purchases to subscriptions.
- **2019–Present — Outside funding and expansion:** After 14 years of bootstrapping, 1Password raised a $200 million Series A led by Accel in November 2019. Acquisitions like SecretHub in 2021 pushed the app further into developer infrastructure, SSH key management, and enterprise security.

