## Major Updates

| Version | Years | What Changed |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **1Password 4** | 2013 | Redesigned for iOS 7 and introduced **Watchtower** to flag leaked, weak, or reused passwords. |
| **1Password 6** | 2016 | Added hosted cloud accounts, family and team vault sharing, and **Travel Mode** to temporarily hide vaults when traveling. |
| **1Password 7** | 2018 | Brought native dark mode, deeper iOS/macOS system autofill, Markdown formatting in secure notes, and better browser integration. |
| **1Password 8** | 2021–2022 | Rebuilt the apps around a shared Rust core with **Quick Access**, system-wide desktop autofill, and cloud-only vault syncing (dropping local Dropbox/WLAN sync). |
| **Passkeys** | 2023–2024 | Added full support for creating, saving, and syncing passkeys across devices, plus unlocking 1Password itself without a master password. |
| **8.12.x** | 2025–2026 | Added `op environment` secret injection to the CLI, post-quantum passkey support, better split-screen login detection, and sign-in support for AI tools like Claude. |

---

## Security & Developer Notes

- **Secret Key:** Combines your account password with a locally generated 128-bit Secret Key so server breaches cannot expose your vault data.
- **CLI (`op`):** Lets you pull credentials and environment variables straight into terminal sessions and scripts instead of storing plain-text `.env` files.
- **Post-Quantum Passkeys:** Uses post-quantum cryptographic algorithms for passkey authentication to guard against future decryption attacks.
